@startuml
title Interaction 2 — Register Arrival (UC07; design only)
hide footbox
skinparam sequenceMessageAlign center
actor AdministrativeStaff as Staff
boundary ":ClinicCLI" as UI
control ":ArrivalController" as Controller
control ":AccessPolicy" as Access
entity "appointments:AppointmentBook" as Book
entity "a:Appointment" as Appointment
control ":ClinicClock" as Clock
control ":UnitOfWork" as Tx
entity ":AuditLog" as Audit
Staff -> UI: Select appointment and register arrival
UI -> Controller: registerArrival(appointmentID)
Controller -> Book: get(appointmentID)
Book --> Controller: a (or notFound)
Controller -> Access: requireRole(session, administrativeStaff)
Controller -> Appointment: requireConfirmed()
Controller -> Clock: todayAt(a.location)
Clock --> Controller: clinicDate
Controller -> Appointment: requireDate(clinicDate)
Controller -> Appointment: requireNotArrived()
Controller -> Clock: nowAt(a.location)
Clock --> Controller: arrivalTime
alt checks passed
  group atomic unit of work (failure discards all staged changes)
    Controller -> Tx: begin()
    Controller -> Appointment: stageArrival(arrivalTime, staffID)
    Controller -> Audit: stageRecord(actorID, patientID, registerArrival, success)
    Controller -> Tx: commit()
  end
  Controller --> UI: appointmentID, arrivalTime, status = confirmed
  UI --> Staff: Arrival registered
else validation, authorisation, or missing appointment
  Controller -> Audit: recordDeniedAttempt(actorID, patientID?, failureCode)
  Controller --> UI: failureCode (original arrivalTime for alreadyArrived)
  UI --> Staff: Show failure without changing appointment
end
note over Controller,Audit
Checks fail fast in contract O05 order; no mutation occurs before validation.
Audit/commit failure rolls back arrival and staff association (auditUnavailable/systemError).
This is a proposed design, not implemented by the iteration-2 scheduling PoC.
end note
@enduml
